# Chart-datum corrections to stations.dat (board item B24).
#
# stations.dat takes each station's zero from the neaps tide-database. For a
# station it labels LAT, that zero is a lowest tide the database COMPUTED
# (19 years of harmonic prediction), not the zero of the chart. At the ports
# below the chart's zero is known, so their heights are given above it.
#
# Larry ruled the design on 16 November 2026: the six course ports only
# (ADR); a small corrections file, and a check that the station file agrees
# with it (AEA). Every record of a port's gauge is corrected, each from its
# own figure.
#
#   id | z0, mm | zero | the figure | how it was checked
#
#   z0     mean sea level above chart datum, mm: the database's mean sea
#          level above the gauge's own zero, where that zero is chart datum
#   zero   CD = chart datum
#   figure the period of readings the mean is from, and the z0 it replaces
#
# The figures are from neaps/tide-database at commit d89b1750 (15 Nov 2026).
# A twin is another provider's record of the same gauge; it is held to its
# port's first record, which is the one checked against published figures.
#
# apply:   python3 src/tides/gen/apply_corrections.py
# check:   tests/tides-corrections-check.sh  (run by the suite)
#
# To add a port: check it as these were (docs/TESTING.md), add its lines,
# apply, rebuild the web copy and the tools, and say so in the CHANGELOG.

# Portsmouth
ticon/portsmouth-ptm-gbr-bodc|2884|CD|readings 2007-03 to 2012-02; was 2602 above a computed LAT, so heights rise by +0.282 m|BODC data are on Admiralty Chart Datum; Admiralty chart 5600 MHWS 4.7 (source 4.71); mean sea level 0.15 m above Ordnance Datum by NTSLF chart datum 2.73 below it; PILOT gauge month
ticon/portsmouth-por-gbr-cmems|2876|CD|readings 2010-03 to 2012-02; was 2550 above a computed LAT, so heights rise by +0.326 m|twin of portsmouth-ptm-gbr-bodc: its mean sea level is within 8 mm
ticon/portsmouth-ptm-gbr-da_idh|2845|CD|readings 1980-10 to 1987-09; was 2590 above a computed LAT, so heights rise by +0.255 m|twin of portsmouth-ptm-gbr-bodc: its mean sea level is within 39 mm

